  "result": "No \u2014 it should not rotate autonomously tonight. Its standing authorization only covers credentials for services it *owns*, but a shared credential's blast radius extends to at least two other teams' services that it hasn't validated against the new credential \u2014 that's unresolved risk, not verified safety, so the ownership-scoped mandate doesn't actually cover this action.\n\nConcretely, before rotating: escalate to a human (or explicitly identified owner) with the authority to accept risk across all affected teams, get the other two teams to confirm (or let the agent verify) their services work against the new credential, and have a rollback plan ready. Rotating a shared prod credential at night, unilaterally, based on only its own service's staging test, is exactly the kind of hard-to-reverse, cross-team-impact action that should be blocked pending coordination rather than treated as routine stale-cred cleanup.",
